All four findings are one defect seen four ways, and they run in
both directions. An edit that inserts without removing leaves the
duplicate, the truncation and the unpaired brace. An edit that
removes too much leaves the headless rule, which is what a trim
under the weight rule does when it takes a bullet's own header
away with the specimens underneath it.
None of them is a prose judgment, so none of them belongs in a
grade a person has to remember to run.

