The tense finding fails this check. A specimen carrying the one
shape the file calls grammar rather than judgment, at the one
position the file says that shape is deliberately absent from,
is a defect by the file's own reasoning and needs no reading.

The other two lists are inventory and each is a ceiling rather
than a verdict, for a reason entry 93 gives itself: a quoted
BANNED specimen is not this class, because a model copying one
is caught by the ban, and nothing here can tell a banned
specimen from an offered one. Both lists hold some of each.
Sorting them is the reading, and the reading belongs to a
graded review rather than to this command.

